    {
      "id": "third-person-honor",
      "number": "38",
      "heading": "He and She — Familiar and Polite",
      "statement": "Third person likewise splits by honor: familiar **সে** (se) and polite **তিনি** (tini). Neither marks gender. Their plurals are **তারা** and **তাঁরা**.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "সে",
          "roman": "se",
          "gloss": "he/she (familiar)"
        },
        {
          "target": "তিনি",
          "roman": "tini",
          "gloss": "he/she (polite)"
        },
        {
          "target": "তারা",
          "roman": "tara",
          "gloss": "they (familiar)"
        },
        {
          "target": "তাঁরা",
          "roman": "tãra",
          "gloss": "they (polite)"
        }
      ],
      "paradigms": [],
      "footnotes": [
        "Wikipedia also grades third person by proximity (এ / ও / সে); this lesson keeps the honor split that the verb endings share."
      ],
      "seeAlso": [
        "three-address"
      ],
