    {
      "id": "pronoun-objective",
      "number": "41",
      "heading": "Objective Forms",
      "statement": "The objective (accusative/dative) of the personal pronouns takes **-কে** (or **-রে** in much of Bangladesh): **আমাকে**, **তোকে**, **তোমাকে**, **আপনাকে**, **তাকে**, **তাঁকে**. Plural objectives are built on the genitive plural: আমাদেরকে, তোমাদেরকে, and so on.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "আমাকে দাও",
          "roman": "amake dao",
          "gloss": "give (it) to me"
        },
        {
          "target": "তাঁকে বলো",
          "roman": "tãke bolo",
          "gloss": "tell him/her (polite)"
        }
      ],
      "paradigms": [
